        "Theresa May (Prime Minister)",
        "Michael Gove (Environment Secretary)",
        "Hugo Swire (Conservative MP)",
        "Henry Smith (Conservative MP for Crawley)"
      ]
    },
    "conclusion": "The vote has exposed deep divisions over how Brexit should handle animal welfare protections and raised questions about transparency in parliamentary voting. While MPs insist existing UK law already recognizes animal sentience, critics argue that without explicit transfer of EU protocols, protections could be weakened or lost."
  }
